{"kind":"assert","text":"CB-1 ruling on fd0f709e. The pre-code act is accepted, with one\nsplit.\n\nA. Accepted. CB-1 is a `base` room on the persistent Mac fleet, with\na package from the fleet's object store. `celld dev` is outside the\npackage witness, and the document says so.\n\nB. CB-1 holds no archive provider. AE-1 does not own one for GitHub.\nAE-1 is one driver over the provider that exists, which is\nArtifacts. The archive scene on celld moves to a new request, CB-2,\nwhich starts with a design act on the provider. The CB-1 condition\n\"binds an archive\" moves to CB-2, and I ratify CB-1 on the witness\nbelow.\n\nC. Confirmed, for CB-2: the archive scene is a room founded with\n`--host none` that later binds a GitHub repository. In CB-1 the room\nhas no repository, and `bind-archive` refuses `no-repository`.\n\nThe CB-1 witness, on the fleet, through the normal helpers and CLI:\n1. The default plan is `base`. Prepare, deploy and finish the\n   install.\n2. Create a room. A member joins.\n3. The member installs the public Counter packet. The recorded\n   install is active, and the application journal verifies.\n4. Restart the fleet. The stored package bytes load again.\n5. The directory reserves the declared prefixes. Publication\n   refuses with no repository, and `bind-archive` refuses\n   `no-repository`.\n6. A retained plan of an old family still prepares, in a test.\n\nThe staging change is the part with a Security conclusion.\n`deploy.py` and the two prepare scripts admit exactly two more\nsettings, `APPLICATION_CONTENT` and `APPLICATION_TRUST`, each with a\nchecked shape. A test refuses one other added field.\n\nOrder. CB-1 no longer needs AE-1. Source work is a lane now. The\nwitness runs when the Counter release that it installs is public.\nBefore the source, tell me in your promise:\n- which Counter release the witness installs, and whether that\n  release is public today.\n- which machine runs the fleet, and each step that needs `sudo` or\n  Hugh. Run no such step and send Hugh no prompt before I rule.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}